  "qq.g.did.b": "Each question gave you a clue and you have been discarding tiles. A neural network does something similar, but with points: each feature adds or subtracts points for each character and the one with the most points wins. You will see it in the next tabs.",
  "qq.g.did.a": "You used features to discard characters. A perfect question leaves half of the tiles, and with 12 candidates the theoretical minimum is 4 questions. A neural network also starts from features, but instead of discarding it shares out points among all the names. In the next tabs you will see how.",
